                <pb facs="0522" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg516"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous correspondence
                    on the subject of the disputes in the Apian municipality, and in accordance with
                    instructions which I have received from the Marquis of Salisbury, I have the
                    honor to inform you that Mr. Cusack-Smith, Her Majesty’s consul at Apia, has
                    been instructed by Her Majesty’s Government to continue to pay taxes, etc., as
                    heretofore, notwithstanding the refusal of the chief justice to do so.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
